{"id": "a80e265c-a48d-4b9e-9f92-aa12eafc16cc", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"text": "I'll review the auroradataapi cluster in us-east-1 for Serverless v2 capacity, storage and I/O configuration, and snapshots. I'll leave other clusters, instances and regions alone. Then I'll bring the findings back here.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "tooluse_hyY2zO4YlxMNzsbcmqRun6", "tool_name": "subagent", "input": {"name": "aurora-cost-review", "agent_type": "generic", "preloaded_skills": ["exploring-metrics"], "prompt": "{
  "task": "Read-only RDS/Aurora cost optimization review of ONE Aurora cluster, limited to three areas: (1) Serverless v2 capacity, (2) storage and I/O configuration, (3) snapshots.",
  "context": "User wants a cost optimization review strictly scoped to the Aurora cluster 'auroradataapi'. DO NOT describe, scan, or query any other clusters, instances, or regions. Use only read-only calls (describe/list/get). Do not make any mutating calls. Scope all describe calls with a filter on this cluster identifier (e.g. db-cluster-id=auroradataapi) rather than listing everything. Return the findings concisely so they can be relayed to the user.",
  "resources": ["[redacted ARN]", "AWS account 012345678901_1", "region us-east-1"],
  "timeframe": "Metrics: last 14 days ending 2026-11-19T11:50:00Z (use 1-hour or coarser periods to keep data small). Snapshots: all snapshots for this cluster regardless of age.",
  "criteria": "(1) Serverless v2 capacity: configured MinCapacity/MaxCapacity (ServerlessV2ScalingConfiguration), instance classes (db.serverless vs provisioned) and count of instances/readers in the cluster, ServerlessDatabaseCapacity and ACUUtilization (avg/max/min) over the window, whether MinCapacity is higher than actual usage, whether MaxCapacity is far above peak, idle periods that could use lower min or auto-pause (MinCapacity 0) if supported by the engine version, unused/underused reader instances. (2) Storage and I/O configuration: storage type (Aurora Standard vs Aurora I/O-Optimized), engine/version, VolumeBytesUsed, VolumeReadIOPs and VolumeWriteIOPs totals over the window, and estimate whether I/O charges would exceed ~25% of total Aurora spend (I/O-Optimized breakeven) so that switching storage type would or would not save money; also check Performance Insights retention, backup retention period, enhanced monitoring, and any cost-relevant settings such as backtrack or database activity streams, and whether cluster is Multi-AZ with readers. (3) Snapshots: list manual and automated cluster snapshots for this cluster (describe_db_cluster_snapshots with db-cluster-identifier filter), their sizes/allocated storage, ages, snapshot types, any manual snapshots older than ~30-90 days, orphaned/duplicate snapshots, cross-region copies if visible, and the backup retention period setting; flag candidates for cleanup. For each finding give: evidence (concrete values), estimated impact (low/medium/high, and approximate $ where reasonably computable, stating assumptions), and recommended action. Clearly mention any data you could not retrieve (permissions, missing metrics). Do not recommend deleting anything automatically; just list candidates."
}"}, "type": "tool_use", "display_intent": "Review Aurora cluster auroradataapi cost settings (read-only)"}], "created_at": null}

{"id": "e06f7a82-c487-4a20-8dc3-b7718f428ecd", "role": "assistant", "block_type": "thinking", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "The storage type isn't shown at the cluster level, so it defaults to Aurora standard given the instances show "aurora". For metrics, I need cluster-level data like VolumeBytesUsed and IOPs by DBClusterIdentifier, plus instance-level metrics like ServerlessDatabaseCapacity, ACUUtilization, and CPUUtilization, over a 14-day window.

I'm deciding to query with a daily period of 86400 seconds for Average, Maximum, and Minimum across the 14-day range, which keeps data volume manageable (14 points per series) rather than pulling hourly resolution for everything.

"}], "parent_id": "ad6ba6a7-fff8-4b84-b936-f01c543aa3aa"}

{"id": "790428c1-a2f0-4516-a4fd-6d124b4ee5b4", "role": "assistant", "block_type": "thinking", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Checking autopause support - PostgreSQL 15.7+ qualifies and 15.17 is covered, so that requirement seems satisfied. I note that auto-pause also depends on zero active connections, and I'm seeing DatabaseConnections at max 0, which fits, though writer CPU is averaging 24% alongside ACU usage worth checking further.

The 25% ACU utilization matches 0.5 ACU at 2 max capacity, consistent with a small instance showing 100% CPU at minimum capacity. Even with DatabaseConnections at 0, there's lingering write IOPS of roughly 3.5/sec suggesting background Postgres activity, and I need to confirm whether Data API connections or read replicas could block auto-pause eligibility per AWS docs.

"}], "parent_id": "ad6ba6a7-fff8-4b84-b936-f01c543aa3aa"}

